.TH MU2EDAQ-BIGREDBOX 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-bigredbox \- Mu2e DAQ critical alert listener ("Big Red Box")
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox
.br
.B python \-m mu2edaq_bigredbox
.br
.B python3 daq_alert.py
(from a checkout)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox
listens for JSON critical\-error alerts broadcast over UDP by Mu2e DAQ
systems and displays a prominent always\-on\-top PyQt6 alert window for
each one, reading the alert aloud.  It is normally started as a background
daemon by the control room via
.BR crs-app (1)
using
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1).
.PP
A GUI environment is required; on Linux the
.B DISPLAY
environment variable must name a display this user may open.
.PP
If the optional
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
package is installed, the listener advertises itself as service
.RB \(dq bigredbox \(dq
so it appears in
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
scans.  Its absence is not an error.
.SS Payload format
Alerts are UTF\-8 JSON datagrams on UDP port 37020:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{"system_id": "DAQ\-NODE\-01",
 "timestamp": "2026\-07\-22T09:15:00",
 "message": "Readout buffer overflow"}
.fi
.RE
.PP
All keys are optional and displayed verbatim; a missing key is shown as
.B UNKNOWN
or
.BR "(no message text)" .
Any JSON object raises an alert.
.PP
The value labels use Qt's automatic text format.
A message that Qt judges to be HTML, for example one containing
.B <
followed by a tag name such as
.BR b ,
.B p
or
.BR font ,
is rendered as rich text, and the text between the angle brackets is not
shown:
.B "rate < b and c > d"
is displayed as
.BR "rate d" .
The spoken text is not affected.
Non\-JSON datagrams and JSON values that are not objects are logged and
ignored.
The format is unversioned and unauthenticated; see
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7).
.SS Alert handling
Each accepted alert opens a window of at least 860\(mu530 pixels, centred and
kept on top.  At most two windows are open at once; further alerts replace
the text of the newest window and are added to its history (click
.B Errors Received
to see it).  Alerts arriving less than 100 ms after the previously accepted
one are dropped and logged; this limit is global, not per sender.
.SS Pausing alerts
Each alert window carries a
.B Pause
checkbox.  While it is ticked the application stops processing incoming alerts
altogether: no new windows open and no open window is updated.  Suppressed
alerts are dropped, not queued, and each one is recorded in the log.
.PP
Pause is global rather than per\-window \(em ticking it on one window
suppresses alerts for all of them.  Processing resumes as soon as no open
window has it ticked, either by unticking it or by closing that window.
There is no timeout.
.SS Text\-to\-speech
Each alert is read aloud when it is accepted (that is, after the pause and
rate\-limit checks), using a template selected by the alert's
.B system_id
(see
.BR DAQ_ALERT_TTS_TEMPLATE_FILE
and
.BR tts_templates.yaml (5)).
Two interchangeable backends are available, selected by
.BR DAQ_ALERT_TTS_BACKEND :
.TP
.I qt
(default) \(em the local Qt
.B QTextToSpeech
plugin.  Rate, volume, voice and plugin selection are configured via
.BR DAQ_ALERT_TTS_RATE ", " DAQ_ALERT_TTS_VOLUME ", " DAQ_ALERT_TTS_VOICE ", and " DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENGINE .
On Linux it needs
.B speech\-dispatcher
or
.BR flite .
.TP
.I aws
\(em AWS Polly, synthesized over the network and played back through
QtMultimedia.  Requires the
.I aws
extra
.RB ( "pip install .[aws]" )
and AWS credentials resolvable via boto3's default chain (environment,
.IR ~/.aws/credentials ,
or an IAM role).  Voice and engine tier are configured via
.BR DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_VOICE " and " DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_ENGINE ;
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_RATE / _VOLUME / _VOICE / _ENGINE
are Qt\-specific and not used by this backend.
.PP
Switching backends is a restart\-time configuration choice, not a live
toggle.
There is no fallback from one backend to the other.
.PP
Once the program has started, speech is best\-effort for either backend: a
missing or broken speech plugin, unset or invalid AWS credentials, network
trouble reaching Polly, an unrecognized engine or voice name, or a missing or
malformed template file all degrade to silence (or the built\-in default
template) with a warning, and never stop the alert window from opening.  The
.I qt
backend disables itself for the rest of the run after an engine error; the
.I aws
backend retries on the next alert.
.PP
.B Caveat:
the Qt multimedia and speech modules are imported unconditionally at
startup.  On Linux they need
.I libpulse.so.0
(package
.B pulseaudio\-libs
on EL9).  Without it the program exits with an
.B ImportError
before opening any window, even when
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENABLED
is false.
.PP
Each alert window also carries a
.B Mute Audio
checkbox, independent of
.BR Pause :
while ticked it silences speech only \(em the alert window still opens and
updates normally.  Like Pause, it is global rather than per\-window.
.SS Single instance
The UDP port is bound before the PID file is written, and the program exits
with status 3 if the bind fails.
.PP
On Linux the bind does not fail when another copy of this program holds the
port, because both set
.BR SO_REUSEADDR ;
a second listener starts normally, both receive every broadcast, and only the
newer one receives unicast alerts.  The start script's port probe has the same
blind spot.  Check with
.B "ss \-ulpn 'sport = :37020'"
before starting a listener by hand.  On macOS the second instance exits with
status 3.
.PP
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1)
falls back to the process holding the UDP port when the PID file is missing,
so a listener started by hand can still be stopped.
.SS Security
There is no authentication.  Any host that can send a UDP datagram to the
listener's port can raise an alert window and have arbitrary text spoken, and
a sender emitting more than ten datagrams per second suppresses alerts from
all other senders through the global rate limit.  The design assumes a closed
DAQ network.
.SS Discovery response
In reply to a DISCOVER request the listener announces its package version in
the
.B version
field and the runtime detail below under
.BR meta ,
so an operator can confirm what is deployed on a node without logging into it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{"app": "bigredbox", "name": "Big Red Box Alerts",
 "port": 37020, "scheme": "udp", "version": "2.0.0",
 "meta": {"version": "2.0.0", "qt": "6.11.0", "pyqt": "6.11.0",
          "python": "3.12.1", "udp_port": "37020"}}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query it with:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2edaq\-discover \-\-filter app=bigredbox \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.SS Signals
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop the UDP listener, the discovery responder and speech, remove the PID
file and exit cleanly.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  All configuration is through the environment (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/daq_alert.pid
PID file written after the port is bound and removed on clean shutdown.
.TP
.I /tmp/daq_alert.log
Application log.  Every received datagram is logged.  Not rotated.
.TP
.I config/tts_templates.yaml
Spoken\-text templates, relative to the current directory; see
.BR tts_templates.yaml (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
UDP port to listen on.  Exported by the control room from
.IR apps.yaml .
Takes precedence over the built\-in default of 37020.  A blank, non\-numeric
or out\-of\-range value is ignored with a warning and the default is used,
so a malformed
.I apps.yaml
entry cannot stop the listener starting.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_LOG_FILE
Log file path.  Defaults to
.IR /tmp/daq_alert.log ,
which is shared by every user on the machine; set this when more than one
operator runs the listener on the same node.  If the log cannot be opened the
program logs to standard error instead of failing.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_PID_FILE
PID file path.  Defaults to
.IR /tmp/daq_alert.pid .
If it cannot be written the listener carries on without it \(em it already
owns the UDP port, and
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh
can still find it by port.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display to open alert windows on.  Required on Linux.
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Qt platform plugin.
.I offscreen
runs without a display (used by the tests; windows are invisible).
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENABLED
Whether alerts are read aloud.  Accepts 1/0, true/false, yes/no, on/off
(case\-insensitive).  Defaults to
.BR true .
An unrecognized value is ignored with a warning and the default is used.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_BACKEND
Which engine reads alerts aloud:
.I qt
(the local Qt
.B QTextToSpeech
plugin) or
.I aws
(AWS Polly, requires the
.I aws
extra \(em
.B "pip install .[aws]"
\(em and network access).  Defaults to
.IR qt .
An unrecognized value is ignored with a warning and the default is used.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_RATE
Speech rate, in Qt's
.B QTextToSpeech.setRate()
range: \-1.0 (slowest) to 1.0 (fastest), 0.0 is normal speed.  Unset or
out\-of\-range leaves the engine's own default.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_VOLUME
Speech volume, in Qt's
.B QTextToSpeech.setVolume()
range: 0.0 to 1.0.  Unset or out\-of\-range leaves the engine's own default.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_VOICE
Case\-insensitive substring match against the
.B name()
of a voice in
.BR QTextToSpeech.availableVoices() .
Unset, or no match found, leaves the engine's default voice.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENGINE
Forces a specific Qt text\-to\-speech plugin (for example
.I speechd
or
.I flite
on Linux,
.I sapi
on Windows,
.I darwin
on macOS) when more than one is available.  Unset lets Qt auto\-pick.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_TEMPLATE_FILE
Path to a YAML file mapping
.B system_id
glob patterns to spoken\-text templates.  Defaults to
.IR config/tts_templates.yaml ,
resolved relative to the current directory.  A missing file is ignored
silently; an unreadable or malformed one is ignored with a warning.  In both
cases the listener falls back to its built\-in default template.  Shared by
both TTS backends.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_VOICE
AWS Polly voice ID (for example
.IR Joanna " or " Matthew ).
Defaults to
.IR Joanna .
Only used when
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_BACKEND
is
.IR aws .
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_ENGINE
AWS Polly engine tier:
.IR standard ", " neural ", or " generative
\(em a voice quality/cost axis, unrelated to
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENGINE
above (which selects a Qt platform plugin).  Defaults to
.IR neural .
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_REGION
AWS region for the Polly client.  Unset lets boto3 resolve it from the
environment or
.IR ~/.aws/config .
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_TTS_AWS_PROFILE
Named AWS profile (from
.I ~/.aws/credentials
or
.IR ~/.aws/config )
to use for the Polly client.  Unset uses boto3's default credential chain.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown (the Qt event loop's exit code).
.TP
.B 1
Python exception at startup, for example a missing shared library such as
.IR libpulse.so.0 .
.TP
.B 3
The UDP port could not be bound, meaning another process holds it.  On Linux
this is not reported when the holder is another
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox
(see
.BR "Single instance" ).
.TP
.B 134
Qt could not open a display (no
.BR DISPLAY ,
no X server, or no permission) and aborted.  This happens before the port is
bound.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2edaq\-bigredbox
.fi
.RE
.PP
Listen on a non\-default port:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
CRS_PORT_UDP=37030 mu2edaq\-bigredbox
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run without speech, logging to a private file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
DAQ_ALERT_TTS_ENABLED=0 DAQ_ALERT_LOG_FILE=~/daq_alert.log mu2edaq\-bigredbox
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1),
.BR tts_templates.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7),
.BR libdaq_alert (3),
.BR daq_alert (3)
